1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,520
[Disclaimer: All events
depicted in this series are fictional]

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:02,350
[and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,260
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:26,910
[Ubon Ratchathani, 2027]

5
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,990
If anything feels unsafe,

6
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:49,840
just get out of there right away.

7
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,990
It's just a regular abandoned building.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,360
Nothing to be afraid of.

9
00:00:56,070 --> 00:00:56,900
Well...

10
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:59,430
are there any vengeful spirits?

11
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:10,710
Just a few.

12
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,460
I heard that

13
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:13,940
the owner is renovating it

14
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,289
into a community health center.

15
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:16,860
If so,

16
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,320
please pass along my blessings as well.

17
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,110
[Peem]

18
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:22,539
Sure. I'll finish up the ritual

19
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:23,840
and be right back.

20
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:26,750
Take your time, Peem.

21
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,620
Your safety matters more than anything.

22
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:32,250
Then I'll miss out on your cooking.

23
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,060
In that case...

24
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:38,420
hurry back, okay?

25
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,200
I'll get dinner ready
and wait for you at our home.

26
00:01:43,289 --> 00:01:43,950
Alright.

27
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,900
See you at our home.

28
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:47,840
See you.

29
00:02:08,229 --> 00:02:09,050
Thong.

30
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:10,840
Ake.

31
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:13,860
I'm getting married next month.

32
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:17,860
Your master won't be lonely anymore.

33
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,260
Don't you worry.

34
00:02:30,990 --> 00:02:31,770
Hello, Coach Dol.

35
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:34,240
Khem, I just sent you
the final episode script.

36
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:34,850
Okay.

37
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:37,000
I'll read it right away.

38
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:38,160
Thank you.

39
00:02:38,410 --> 00:02:39,210
Will do.

40
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:41,010
Okay.

41
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:38,650
[Incanting]

42
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:47,700
[Incanting]

43
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:48,670
Is it done yet?

44
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:51,329
Like I'd know, Auntie.

45
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,840
If you don't know, then go check.

46
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,320
And I'm not an auntie.

47
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:57,260
Yeah, but a Karen.

48
00:03:58,220 --> 00:03:59,710
Go check. Now.

49
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:01,560
Just go.

50
00:04:03,650 --> 00:04:04,310
Hurry.

51
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,060
You done yet, bro?

52
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:18,760
Why did you come in here?

53
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,890
I'm going to help you pack.

54
00:04:58,159 --> 00:05:04,250
♪ A blessed day has come,
with fortune aglow ♪

55
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:10,320
♪ Graceful offerings
are arranged in a row ♪

56
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:14,570
♪ Sacred threads and rings of gold, ♪

57
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:17,470
♪ Jewels and necklaces,
precious to behold ♪

58
00:05:17,490 --> 00:05:19,710
♪ A feast overflowing
with plenty to spare ♪

59
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,550
♪ All things prepared
with the greatest care ♪

60
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,120
♪ Betel rolls and areca nuts
are laid there ♪

61
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:28,120
♪ Everything adorned
and displayed with flair ♪

62
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:34,190
♪ "May your vital forces come forth" ♪

63
00:05:34,210 --> 00:05:38,320
♪ May your vital forces come forth ♪

64
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:42,600
♪ O vital forces, beyond the skies, ♪

65
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:44,840
♪ In distant realms
where your souls fly, ♪

66
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:46,659
♪ Heed the call and now arise, ♪

67
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:53,490
♪ Return to where your vessels lie ♪

68
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:35,940
I'm here, babe.

69
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,590
Walk straight on in.

70
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:44,740
What?

71
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:04,670
- It's a test
- It's a test

72
00:07:04,690 --> 00:07:06,690
- of your sixth sense.
- of your sixth sense.

73
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,860
- Guess
- Guess

74
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:10,230
- which one of us
- which one of us

75
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:12,180
- is your boyfriend.
- is your boyfriend.

76
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,920
I don't need any sixth sense for this.

77
00:07:30,130 --> 00:07:31,880
I know every inch of you, Jet.

78
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,280
I can tell with just my heart.

79
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,020
Hey.

80
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,200
Take it easy.

81
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:05,860
We're not alone, you know.

82
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:09,690
Alright.

83
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,630
Thank you so much, everyone.

84
00:08:11,650 --> 00:08:13,340
You can all get back to work now.

85
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:16,860
What's with that smile?

86
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,140
The durian looks amazing.

87
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,190
Let's head inside.

88
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:20,880
Okay.

89
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:23,110
Jet and Charn

90
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:25,380
are both an essential part
of this story.

91
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:27,470
They're friends
who have sacrificed so much

92
00:08:28,050 --> 00:08:31,010
and braved countless dangers
for me unconditionally.

93
00:08:32,289 --> 00:08:32,950
Come on.

94
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,260
Whoa.

95
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:42,190
Look.

96
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,500
We're here.

97
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:48,130
Welcome to my orchard home,

98
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:49,550
bae.

99
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,810
Though the two
seem like polar opposites...

100
00:08:55,830 --> 00:08:56,780
Let's go inside.

101
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,270
- They complement each other perfectly,
- Let's go.

102
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,990
and that's how their love blossomed.

103
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:06,200
[Grandpa Phaew's Durian Orchard]

104
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,510
As for Master Paran,

105
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:16,700
on the outside, he may appear stern,

106
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:18,760
cold, and indifferent to anyone...

107
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:20,910
I know you spirits are still conscious.

108
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:27,040
Do not let vengeance consume your souls.

109
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,900
You have lingered here for so long

110
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:40,210
that you have forgotten
who you truly are.

111
00:09:42,570 --> 00:09:44,140
Yet in truth, it is Master

112
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:46,870
who cares the most deeply
for everyone around him.

113
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,360
Let me set you free.

114
00:09:56,120 --> 00:10:03,740
[Incanting]

115
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,620
May you pass on to a peaceful realm.

116
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:08,530
May every life and every soul

117
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:10,730
imprisoned in this place

118
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:15,380
be reborn into a blessed realm.

119
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:21,160
His back bears the weight
of everything all the time.

120
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,700
He wants every struggle

121
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:26,760
to end with
as little heartbreak as possible

122
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:30,440
without ever caring

123
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:33,500
how much pain he inflicts upon himself.

124
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,220
That is why,

125
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:44,230
no matter how stern
he appears on the outside...

126
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:48,100
May you pass on to a peaceful realm.

127
00:10:49,410 --> 00:10:51,200
Let your karma guide your path now.

128
00:10:51,370 --> 00:10:53,120
There's always a hint of vulnerability

129
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:56,510
in his eyes
that makes your heart ache.

130
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,590
Now that you're done helping the ghosts,

131
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:04,840
help your friend too, damn it.

132
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,670
Hurry up, it hurts.

133
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:28,920
I think

134
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:31,490
if we can preserve
the essence of the characters,

135
00:11:32,310 --> 00:11:34,350
the audience is bound to love them.

136
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,610
And if we need to adapt things
for the series,

137
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:39,950
I'm sure the audience will understand.

138
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:42,600
Okay, thank you so much, Khem.

139
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:47,320
By the way,
when's your wedding with Master?

140
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:53,350
Probably early next year, Coach Dol.

141
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:55,290
Oh, so it's just around the corner.

142
00:11:55,310 --> 00:11:56,610
Congratulations.

143
00:11:57,970 --> 00:11:59,120
Thank you so much.

144
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:02,680
I hope everything goes smoothly on set.

145
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:05,850
Alright, I'll call again
if I need more advice.

146
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:07,710
Sure. Goodbye.

147
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,310
Thank you.

148
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:23,370
I missed you so much, Peem.

149
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:25,840
I've barely been gone a day.

150
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:26,920
You missed me already?

151
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:36,010
Yeah, you're so dramatic.

152
00:13:36,490 --> 00:13:37,740
Don't you miss me at all?

153
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:41,960
Jet, Charn!

154
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:46,350
It's been so long.

155
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:52,980
[Only for someone special]

156
00:13:57,590 --> 00:14:00,010
Whoa, Master's place

157
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,670
is now tightly fenced in and secured.

158
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:04,660
Well, it's because of
that break-in last time.

159
00:14:04,690 --> 00:14:06,420
Oh, back when we went back
for our final year,

160
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,770
and someone was hitting on you?

161
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:10,670
Master even left his house

162
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:12,100
just to be with you
because he was jealous.

163
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:14,050
Did that really call
for building a whole fence?

164
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:17,770
No need to rub it in.

165
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:22,150
Let's just head inside.

166
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:24,640
Or you'll end up leaving late.

167
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:33,060
Come on, let's head inside.

168
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,570
Wait a second.

169
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:37,630
Why did you guys buy so much stuff?

170
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:38,300
- I went all out.
- Look!

171
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:40,360
Here, check this out.

172
00:14:46,450 --> 00:14:47,190
Whoa!

173
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,250
Did you embroider this yourself, Khem?

174
00:14:50,650 --> 00:14:51,590
Thanks a lot.

175
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:52,710
Yeah.

176
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,840
Master even put an amulet inside.

177
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:56,380
- Open it up.
- Really?

178
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,690
- How is it?
- Whoa.

179
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:04,350
An inn-khu.

180
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:07,500
It carries sacred blessings

181
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,660
that will keep your love strong
for years to come.

182
00:15:10,890 --> 00:15:13,360
No matter what you have to face,

183
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:15,630
you must hold hands
and get through it together.

184
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:36,540
What?

185
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:41,040
Khem...

186
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:44,700
What is this?

187
00:15:45,130 --> 00:15:46,040
Check it out.

188
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:48,840
Is it a gift?

189
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,730
Whoa.

190
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,340
So cute!

191
00:15:58,150 --> 00:16:00,250
You're giving me two of them?

192
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,350
It's so you can wear them with Master.

193
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:03,520
They're adorable.

194
00:16:07,170 --> 00:16:09,060
If you put them on, send me a picture.

195
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:10,320
Okay.

196
00:16:13,670 --> 00:16:14,630
Aren't they cute?

197
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,990
There's more?

198
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:31,110
Oh, I guess it comes as a set.

199
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:43,690
Well, since marriage is all about
starting a family...

200
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,110
As for their future,

201
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,580
I think it's best
to let them decide for themselves.

202
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,020
Sorry about that.

203
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:53,630
Was I being rude?

204
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:01,150
Don't overthink it.

205
00:17:01,530 --> 00:17:02,130
Come on.

206
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:03,760
Let's just eat.

207
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:05,650
Come on.

208
00:17:05,670 --> 00:17:07,060
- Okay.
- Let's dig in.

209
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,760
- Hey.
- Come on.

210
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,349
Let's have a toast.

211
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,740
Three, two, one...

212
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,550
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

213
00:17:16,579 --> 00:17:18,000
Whoa.

214
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:32,930
Did they make the bottle's mouth wider?

215
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:34,490
- Yeah.
- Right?

216
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:37,000
It makes the drink smell better, Jet.

217
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:37,980
Totally.

218
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:52,700
Whoa...

219
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:55,470
What?

220
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:57,790
Your cheeks smell better, too.

221
00:17:58,970 --> 00:17:59,860
Charn!

222
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:09,350
- Open wide.
- Ah...

223
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,610
Eat up

224
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:13,090
so you'll have
plenty of energy for tonight.

225
00:18:13,870 --> 00:18:14,650
Charn!

226
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,340
Look at Khem.

227
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:22,550
His mouth is open wider
than the bottle now!

228
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:25,940
- Let's just eat.
- Come on.

229
00:18:25,970 --> 00:18:27,870
You're gonna give yourself cancer.
It's charred!

230
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:28,930
Just eat up.

231
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:30,240
Eat some fiber, too.

232
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:35,140
You want me to feed you?

233
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,930
Did they get home already?

234
00:19:12,850 --> 00:19:13,930
What are you doing?

235
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:16,770
I just want to recharge on you.

236
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:22,100
I haven't gotten to since I got back.

237
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,400
If you recharge too much,

238
00:19:30,390 --> 00:19:31,710
you might lose control.

239
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:58,620
Hang in there a little longer.

240
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,740
Once we finally tie the knot

241
00:20:03,350 --> 00:20:04,540
and become family,

242
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,240
we'll get to share a room.

243
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:13,720
Are you telling me that?

244
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,890
I'm telling myself.

245
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:24,220
If it weren't for the auspicious date,

246
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,580
I'd carry you off
to register our marriage right now.

247
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:32,430
That way, you could take my last name.

248
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,800
Your last name?

249
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,650
Why?

250
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:51,470
Is something wrong?

251
00:20:54,850 --> 00:20:55,710
No.

252
00:20:58,410 --> 00:20:59,440
I just...

253
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:02,380
completely forgot
to even think about the surname.

254
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:04,040
You don't want to change it?

255
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,990
I'm sorry.

256
00:21:10,330 --> 00:21:12,500
Whichever last name you want to use,

257
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:15,270
it's totally up to you.

258
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,020
Are you mad at me?

259
00:21:27,230 --> 00:21:28,250
I'm not.

260
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:30,110
It's just that...

261
00:21:31,150 --> 00:21:33,460
I really hadn't thought
about this at all.

262
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:39,070
The reason I've always kept
my mom's surname

263
00:21:40,710 --> 00:21:44,290
is to keep the curse confined
within our bloodline

264
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:50,230
and prevent it
from spreading to another family.

265
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:54,640
You're worried that if you change it,

266
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,440
Auntie Khaekhai's family name
will be lost, right?

267
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,680
Take all the time you need.

268
00:22:17,590 --> 00:22:18,760
We still have time.

269
00:22:28,170 --> 00:22:28,830
Wait...

270
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:32,560
We were talking so much
we missed the countdown.

271
00:22:34,130 --> 00:22:36,670
Happy New Year, Peem.

272
00:22:41,390 --> 00:22:42,850
Happy New Year, Khem.

273
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:46,850
Let's stay together
for a long, long time.

274
00:23:05,450 --> 00:23:06,140
Uh...

275
00:23:06,860 --> 00:23:08,140
Want to watch the fireworks?

276
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:12,700
Whoa.

277
00:23:14,950 --> 00:23:15,890
So pretty.

278
00:23:18,550 --> 00:23:20,430
It's so beautiful, Peem.

279
00:23:27,420 --> 00:23:33,840
♪ Our love
is still right here to stay, ♪

280
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:40,320
♪ It never left, never went away ♪

281
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:46,600
♪ Though it was hard
to get through yesterday, ♪

282
00:23:46,630 --> 00:23:53,120
♪ The sky looks bright again today ♪

283
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,080
That's enough.

284
00:25:03,390 --> 00:25:05,210
Putting in quite a workout
to start the year, huh?

285
00:25:07,030 --> 00:25:08,430
Happy New Year,

286
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:09,630
babe.

287
00:25:13,650 --> 00:25:15,090
Happy New Year,

288
00:25:15,610 --> 00:25:16,630
bae.

289
00:25:59,220 --> 00:26:01,050
You've only been here
for a few days, leaving already?

290
00:26:02,170 --> 00:26:03,510
Can't you stay a little longer?

291
00:26:03,990 --> 00:26:05,060
With you here,

292
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:07,340
my boss looks so much brighter.

293
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:11,790
What do I look like
when he's not around?

294
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:14,920
Excuse me, then.

295
00:26:14,950 --> 00:26:16,010
Thank you.

296
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:25,260
He's got a point, though.

297
00:26:25,630 --> 00:26:27,460
I'm so much happier
when you're around.

298
00:26:29,540 --> 00:26:30,870
Can't you just stay?

299
00:26:34,110 --> 00:26:36,000
I still have a mountain of work
at the hotel.

300
00:26:37,940 --> 00:26:38,960
Wait for me, okay?

301
00:26:39,320 --> 00:26:41,130
I'll be back for Khem's wedding anyway.

302
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:45,830
Let's go.

303
00:27:03,310 --> 00:27:03,930
Mom?

304
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:05,930
Hello.

305
00:27:14,110 --> 00:27:15,050
Come on, Mom.

306
00:27:15,810 --> 00:27:17,660
I was about to bring
Charn over to see you.

307
00:27:17,860 --> 00:27:19,350
You didn't have to come
all the way here.

308
00:27:29,780 --> 00:27:30,880
This one is ripe.

309
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,310
This one isn't ripe yet.

310
00:27:43,330 --> 00:27:44,490
This one's ripe, too.

311
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:53,440
Whoa, this one is too ripe.

312
00:27:53,650 --> 00:27:56,630
Actually, we've already sorted out
the mature ones.

313
00:28:00,690 --> 00:28:02,390
Gosh, Jet...

314
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:04,350
Will you ever get the hang of this?

315
00:28:04,700 --> 00:28:06,930
You can't even tell ripe from unripe.

316
00:28:06,950 --> 00:28:09,430
Come on, Mom, give me some time.

317
00:28:09,450 --> 00:28:11,440
Can you stop using
your teacher mode on your son?

318
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,490
What?

319
00:28:18,660 --> 00:28:19,410
Mom,

320
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:21,830
Jet is really dedicated to the work.

321
00:28:22,020 --> 00:28:23,120
He might not know what he's doing,

322
00:28:23,140 --> 00:28:25,060
but he's putting
his whole heart into it.

323
00:28:25,650 --> 00:28:26,470
Charn!

324
00:28:26,930 --> 00:28:28,070
Do you actually want to help me?

325
00:28:28,840 --> 00:28:30,110
Of course I do.

326
00:28:32,290 --> 00:28:33,070
Yes.

327
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:38,490
Oh, Charn.

328
00:28:38,520 --> 00:28:39,140
Yes?

329
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,920
Didn't you bring my mom a gift?

330
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,200
I'll go grab it for you.

331
00:28:47,180 --> 00:28:49,700
It's probably a Chinese New Year gift.

332
00:28:50,810 --> 00:28:52,470
A Valentine's gift, Mom.

333
00:28:52,490 --> 00:28:53,170
Uh...

334
00:28:55,480 --> 00:28:56,270
Mom,

335
00:28:56,420 --> 00:28:58,590
get to know your future son-in-law
while I'm gone.

336
00:28:58,870 --> 00:29:00,050
Love you, Mom. Muah!

337
00:29:00,070 --> 00:29:00,880
[J3T Ubon Ratchathani 108]

338
00:29:02,470 --> 00:29:03,730
Jet!

339
00:29:06,410 --> 00:29:07,200
He's gone.

340
00:29:07,230 --> 00:29:08,010
He...

341
00:29:08,090 --> 00:29:08,930
just left us.

342
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:16,140
Happy belated New Year, Mom.

343
00:29:16,820 --> 00:29:17,730
This one's ripe, by the way.

344
00:29:33,270 --> 00:29:34,100
Mint.

345
00:29:40,900 --> 00:29:42,150
Praemai.

346
00:29:48,030 --> 00:29:49,140
Peem?

347
00:29:52,790 --> 00:29:53,850
The wedding invites
you're having Charn

348
00:29:53,870 --> 00:29:55,380
hand out to your friends
in Bangkok, right?

349
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:57,300
Yes.

350
00:29:59,750 --> 00:30:01,700
Actually, everyone's already said
they'd come,

351
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:04,430
but since the artwork
turned out so gorgeous,

352
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:06,850
I wanted them
to have the actual cards, too.

353
00:30:08,250 --> 00:30:08,810
You know...

354
00:30:09,630 --> 00:30:11,380
it's pretty rare to see

355
00:30:11,630 --> 00:30:13,130
a smile like that on your face.

356
00:30:29,170 --> 00:30:31,150
I save it just for you.

357
00:31:01,450 --> 00:31:04,860
Khwankhao, Phet and Uea's daughter,

358
00:31:05,380 --> 00:31:07,470
took her friends from Bangkok
trekking in the forest

359
00:31:07,700 --> 00:31:08,980
right before New Year's.

360
00:31:15,370 --> 00:31:16,390
Then Pond,

361
00:31:16,690 --> 00:31:17,840
Baitong's husband,

362
00:31:18,800 --> 00:31:20,200
volunteered to pick them up

363
00:31:20,870 --> 00:31:23,430
but went missing
along with all of them.

364
00:31:26,660 --> 00:31:28,950
Aren't the police
already searching for them?

365
00:31:33,340 --> 00:31:34,510
They are, Master,

366
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,700
but it's been three days now.

367
00:31:37,140 --> 00:31:38,420
Still no sign of them.

368
00:31:39,130 --> 00:31:41,600
Khwankhao knows sorcery herself.

369
00:31:42,190 --> 00:31:43,780
For things
to have turned out like this,

370
00:31:44,010 --> 00:31:45,910
that forest must be no ordinary place.

371
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:48,060
The occult forces must be powerful.

372
00:31:50,390 --> 00:31:51,110
Master,

373
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,220
please help my daughter.

374
00:31:54,590 --> 00:31:56,590
I'll do whatever it takes to repay you.

375
00:31:57,060 --> 00:31:59,030
Please save her, Master.

376
00:32:00,930 --> 00:32:03,070
Whether dead or alive,

377
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:07,240
please let me see her face again.

378
00:32:09,630 --> 00:32:12,110
Please help me, Master.

379
00:32:16,550 --> 00:32:18,020
I'm sorry.

380
00:32:20,860 --> 00:32:22,470
But you should prepare yourselves
for the worst.

381
00:32:26,290 --> 00:32:27,600
It's already been three days.

382
00:32:29,990 --> 00:32:31,800
There's likely not much I can do.

383
00:32:33,850 --> 00:32:35,950
How are you doing, sweetie?

384
00:32:39,120 --> 00:32:40,480
Pond...

385
00:32:43,830 --> 00:32:45,330
Master, please help them.

386
00:32:50,150 --> 00:32:51,300
But...

387
00:32:51,460 --> 00:32:52,660
At least give it a try.

388
00:32:54,210 --> 00:32:56,190
I want you to help everyone here,

389
00:32:57,490 --> 00:32:58,900
just like you once helped me.

390
00:33:04,970 --> 00:33:07,120
Please, Master.

391
00:33:07,350 --> 00:33:09,840
- Please help us.
- We have nowhere else to turn.

392
00:33:09,870 --> 00:33:11,680
Master, please help them.

393
00:34:03,550 --> 00:34:05,120
I'll be back as soon as I can.

394
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:07,380
Okay.

395
00:34:27,469 --> 00:34:28,400
You should go.

396
00:34:39,570 --> 00:34:44,820
[KJ 1726 Ubon Ratchathani]

397
00:34:57,640 --> 00:34:58,270
Oh?

398
00:35:01,100 --> 00:35:03,660
Whoa, Master is performing exorcisms
to start the year?

399
00:35:04,980 --> 00:35:05,950
Kind of.

400
00:35:06,170 --> 00:35:08,170
But why did you ride a motorbike here?

401
00:35:08,710 --> 00:35:09,510
Where's Charn?

402
00:35:12,840 --> 00:35:14,480
He'll be right behind me.

403
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:18,460
I'm starving.

404
00:35:18,550 --> 00:35:19,480
Got anything to eat?

405
00:35:20,300 --> 00:35:21,060
Sure do.

406
00:35:21,610 --> 00:35:23,270
There are pork sausages in the kitchen.

407
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:26,140
Sweet! Pork sausages, here I come.

408
00:35:38,610 --> 00:35:39,490
Coach Dol?

409
00:35:44,510 --> 00:35:45,640
Hello, Coach Dol.

410
00:35:46,330 --> 00:35:48,000
Is there an issue with the script?

411
00:35:53,270 --> 00:35:54,010
What?

412
00:35:55,700 --> 00:35:56,950
The set was haunted,

413
00:35:56,980 --> 00:35:58,790
so you had to call off
three days of shooting?

414
00:36:00,020 --> 00:36:00,780
So,

415
00:36:01,260 --> 00:36:03,050
did anyone else
experience anything strange?

416
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:10,240
In that case,
I think it's likely a vengeful spirit.

417
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:12,370
My advice is

418
00:36:12,480 --> 00:36:14,640
to postpone the shoot for now.

419
00:36:15,200 --> 00:36:16,620
You won't make the air date?

420
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:21,350
You want Master to exorcise the ghosts?

421
00:36:21,950 --> 00:36:22,740
Well...

422
00:36:24,100 --> 00:36:26,270
he just left a moment ago.

423
00:36:31,410 --> 00:36:35,210
His disciples who could do it?

424
00:36:40,660 --> 00:36:43,170
Someone to stand in for him?

425
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:50,590
Let's talk again later, then.

426
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:52,430
Yes.

427
00:36:55,660 --> 00:36:57,070
Why did you hang up so fast?

428
00:36:58,470 --> 00:36:59,910
Why didn't you just say yes?

429
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:01,300
He basically set the stage for me.

430
00:37:03,300 --> 00:37:04,900
This isn't a joke, Jet.

431
00:37:04,920 --> 00:37:05,720
Hey!

432
00:37:06,010 --> 00:37:07,260
I'm not joking, either.

433
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:09,080
I'm Master's number-one disciple,
you know.

434
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:11,040
Come on, please.

435
00:37:11,340 --> 00:37:13,280
We can go bust ghosts together
just like old times.

436
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:15,370
Nobody's more vicious
than Ramphueng anyway.

437
00:37:18,310 --> 00:37:19,050
Oh, and...

438
00:37:19,630 --> 00:37:20,430
that way,

439
00:37:20,740 --> 00:37:22,750
you can hand out
the wedding invitations yourself.

440
00:37:22,780 --> 00:37:24,180
You won't have to trouble Charn.

441
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:33,800
[GP 2543 Ubon Ratchathani]

442
00:37:34,230 --> 00:37:36,380
Why did you run away from your mom, Jet?

443
00:37:37,030 --> 00:37:37,760
Charn?

444
00:37:37,870 --> 00:37:38,580
Oh!

445
00:37:38,900 --> 00:37:39,700
Charn...

446
00:37:39,860 --> 00:37:42,350
Look, there's trouble
on the set of Khem's series.

447
00:37:42,370 --> 00:37:43,860
They need Master's disciples
to exorcise ghosts!

448
00:37:53,220 --> 00:37:54,230
Don't even think about it, Jet.

449
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:57,170
Charn has to get back to work
at the hotel soon.

450
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:05,660
Hello, Mom.

451
00:38:08,910 --> 00:38:09,980
I'll be there a bit late.

452
00:38:14,810 --> 00:38:16,390
Where are they shooting the series?

453
00:38:17,190 --> 00:38:18,110
Where?

454
00:38:19,860 --> 00:38:20,840
Sing Buri.

455
00:38:22,990 --> 00:38:24,640
I have something to do
in Sing Buri, Mom.

456
00:38:24,660 --> 00:38:26,430
I might be delayed by a day or two.

457
00:38:28,560 --> 00:38:29,710
No need to cancel the flight.

458
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:32,920
Could you have your secretary
book two more seats instead?

459
00:38:41,600 --> 00:38:42,930
Go get your stuff!

460
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:43,790
The luggage, you know.

461
00:38:44,970 --> 00:38:46,280
And I have to...

462
00:38:53,460 --> 00:38:54,210
Yes!

463
00:38:57,900 --> 00:38:58,500
Let's go.

464
00:38:58,780 --> 00:39:00,600
Now I have to delay my return,

465
00:39:00,620 --> 00:39:02,050
rebook tickets,

466
00:39:02,070 --> 00:39:03,220
and I still have to...

467
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,190
Eat up!

468
00:39:04,760 --> 00:39:05,910
Come on.

469
00:39:06,340 --> 00:39:07,220
Come on, Khem.

470
00:39:07,460 --> 00:39:08,490
Go take a shower and get ready.

471
00:39:13,750 --> 00:39:15,600
Don't let anything happen to any of you.

472
00:39:17,050 --> 00:39:18,010
Understood?

473
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:21,920
Got it! I won't let even one mosquito
get near Khem.

474
00:39:22,130 --> 00:39:23,680
Don't worry, Master.

475
00:39:23,790 --> 00:39:25,100
If things get dangerous,

476
00:39:25,140 --> 00:39:27,740
I'll get everyone
out of there immediately.

477
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:28,900
Yeah, that's right.

478
00:39:36,260 --> 00:39:36,970
I got it.

479
00:39:37,790 --> 00:39:39,880
Trouble right at the start
of the year, huh?

480
00:39:40,460 --> 00:39:41,440
Tell me about it.

481
00:39:42,500 --> 00:39:44,380
I only left a few hours ago,

482
00:39:44,770 --> 00:39:46,810
and you're already running away from me.

483
00:39:48,850 --> 00:39:49,460
Well...

484
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:52,800
think of it as doing a good deed
before our wedding.

485
00:39:53,690 --> 00:39:55,670
I'm sure our wedding

486
00:39:55,700 --> 00:39:57,200
will go without a hitch.

487
00:39:59,410 --> 00:40:00,810
Wait for me, okay?

488
00:40:02,230 --> 00:40:04,330
I... will make it... back alive...

489
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:05,040
Sorry?

490
00:40:06,220 --> 00:40:07,090
Hello?

491
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:09,880
Hello?

492
00:40:12,490 --> 00:40:13,240
Hello?

493
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:14,540
Hello, Peem?

494
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:15,630
Peem?

495
00:40:15,750 --> 00:40:16,650
Hello?

496
00:40:16,860 --> 00:40:21,160
[KJ 1726 Ubon Ratchathani]

497
00:40:21,610 --> 00:40:22,440
Hello?

498
00:40:34,490 --> 00:40:36,220
What happened, Khem?

499
00:40:42,450 --> 00:40:43,750
He might...

500
00:40:44,350 --> 00:40:46,320
be in a dead zone, I guess.

501
00:40:47,050 --> 00:40:48,420
It's probably nothing.

502
00:40:48,630 --> 00:40:49,270
Right?

503
00:40:54,720 --> 00:40:55,620
This is great.

504
00:40:56,500 --> 00:40:58,670
We haven't all
hung out together in ages.

505
00:40:59,570 --> 00:41:01,570
If you didn't run away from your mom,

506
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:03,970
I doubt we'd be doing this at all.

507
00:41:04,210 --> 00:41:04,970
Hey!

508
00:41:05,510 --> 00:41:07,670
Don't kill the vibe like that, bae.

509
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:09,670
Come on.

510
00:41:09,700 --> 00:41:11,620
Now, hands in.

511
00:41:13,070 --> 00:41:13,720
Okay.

512
00:41:15,090 --> 00:41:16,600
One, two, three!

513
00:41:23,630 --> 00:41:24,770
What are you laughing at?

514
00:41:25,850 --> 00:41:26,770
What's so funny?

515
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:28,680
It's just hilarious.

516
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:40,790
Uncle,

517
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:45,050
you should be with the parents.

518
00:41:45,870 --> 00:41:47,270
You don't need to follow me.

519
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:50,920
Once we reach an area with reception,

520
00:41:51,400 --> 00:41:53,850
call Kachen and tell him where I am.

521
00:41:56,190 --> 00:41:56,810
Sure.

522
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:05,580
That must be his van.

523
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:12,600
[KJ 1726 Ubon Ratchathani]

524
00:42:22,010 --> 00:42:23,460
Oh, Master! Hello.

525
00:42:23,490 --> 00:42:24,210
Hello.

526
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,260
Are you Inspector Wichian?

527
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:27,350
Yes, that's right.

528
00:42:29,720 --> 00:42:31,200
What's the situation?

529
00:42:31,970 --> 00:42:34,600
Well, the last lead that we found

530
00:42:34,620 --> 00:42:35,890
is this vehicle right here.

531
00:42:36,820 --> 00:42:38,730
It was left abandoned here.

532
00:42:39,440 --> 00:42:40,910
The car itself

533
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:43,320
doesn't show any signs
of a collision or damage.

534
00:42:43,380 --> 00:42:46,610
However, judging by the tire marks,

535
00:42:46,810 --> 00:42:48,560
we can reasonably deduce

536
00:42:48,590 --> 00:42:52,250
that the driver must have swerved
to avoid something.

537
00:42:53,630 --> 00:42:54,850
And take a look here.

538
00:42:55,910 --> 00:42:56,800
Footprints.

539
00:42:57,970 --> 00:43:00,840
It looks as though
they were all fleeing from someone

540
00:43:00,910 --> 00:43:02,260
or something.

541
00:43:02,820 --> 00:43:04,650
Has a search team
gone in after them yet?

542
00:43:04,670 --> 00:43:07,800
Well, that's actually
a major issue in itself.

543
00:43:08,080 --> 00:43:08,880
I mean...

544
00:43:09,370 --> 00:43:10,170
Ow!

545
00:43:11,620 --> 00:43:12,420
See?

546
00:43:13,180 --> 00:43:14,080
What's the status?

547
00:43:14,220 --> 00:43:14,980
Inspector,

548
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:17,230
we didn't go far,
but somehow we ended up here again.

549
00:43:18,800 --> 00:43:19,780
Again.

550
00:43:43,800 --> 00:43:44,810
Hurry, Nop!

551
00:43:46,100 --> 00:43:47,290
- Wait, Kao!
- What?

552
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,040
Come here!

553
00:43:48,690 --> 00:43:50,190
We're right back where we started.

554
00:43:51,460 --> 00:43:52,140
Shit!

555
00:43:52,380 --> 00:43:53,600
Are we just gonna stop
and let them get us?

556
00:43:53,620 --> 00:43:54,500
Keep moving!

557
00:43:54,540 --> 00:43:55,150
We can't do that.

558
00:43:55,170 --> 00:43:56,150
We have to go back,

559
00:43:56,180 --> 00:43:57,040
or Max won't make it!

560
00:43:57,070 --> 00:43:58,320
What the hell can we do
if we go back?

561
00:43:58,350 --> 00:44:00,410
They're freaking ghosts.
Let's just get help!

562
00:44:00,430 --> 00:44:01,670
You're not gonna help our friend?

563
00:44:01,690 --> 00:44:03,720
How the hell can we?
We'll all end up dead!

564
00:44:03,740 --> 00:44:05,110
Even if we run,
we'll just end up back here.

565
00:44:05,140 --> 00:44:06,370
- God!
- What's the point of running?

566
00:44:06,400 --> 00:44:08,190
- What the fuck is your problem?
- If you wanna go, then go.

567
00:44:08,210 --> 00:44:09,930
I'm going back to help my friend.

568
00:44:19,290 --> 00:44:20,150
Shit...

569
00:44:37,480 --> 00:44:39,010
- Which way do we go?
- Nop!

570
00:44:40,700 --> 00:44:42,550
- Don't come closer!
- Don't you dare!

571
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:52,810
Om, may success be granted.
May divine blessings be revealed.

572
00:44:52,830 --> 00:44:55,720
I call upon Ganesha in the forms
of Phra Phinek and Phra Phinai,

573
00:44:55,750 --> 00:44:58,150
Shiva, Vishnu,

574
00:44:58,170 --> 00:44:59,940
- Brahma, the Lord of Wind,
- Shit, what's going on?

575
00:44:59,970 --> 00:45:01,800
- the Lords of Water and Fire,
- Shit!

576
00:45:01,830 --> 00:45:04,130
- and Goddess Uma Bhogavati.
- Nop, run!

577
00:45:04,150 --> 00:45:07,050
- Move!
- By whose divine decree,

578
00:45:09,220 --> 00:45:11,550
I hold the power
to unseal heaven and earth,

579
00:45:11,700 --> 00:45:14,090
the seas and mighty oceans,

580
00:45:14,110 --> 00:45:17,480
the mountains and soaring peaks,

581
00:45:17,560 --> 00:45:20,600
and the rivers and flowing streams.

582
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:43,770
Guardian spirits of the forest,

583
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:47,020
do you know where everyone is?

584
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:51,110
Will you make a promise to me first?

585
00:45:52,740 --> 00:45:54,010
What do you ask of me?

586
00:45:54,870 --> 00:45:58,390
Perform an ordination ceremony
for this forest.

587
00:45:59,190 --> 00:46:02,160
Cleanse this land
and restore its purity.

588
00:46:12,440 --> 00:46:13,850
I give you my vow.

589
00:46:14,290 --> 00:46:17,910
Those kids are being hunted
by malicious spirits

590
00:46:17,950 --> 00:46:21,570
that do not belong to this forest.

591
00:46:22,310 --> 00:46:26,630
They are merely thralls of a sorcerer,

592
00:46:26,850 --> 00:46:28,810
conjured solely to hunt them down.

593
00:46:30,810 --> 00:46:32,730
There isn't much time left.

594
00:46:33,110 --> 00:46:36,070
You, too, must tread carefully.

595
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:44,190
Master,

596
00:46:45,880 --> 00:46:47,130
is something wrong?

597
00:46:51,100 --> 00:46:52,630
A sorcerer

598
00:46:53,590 --> 00:46:55,280
has sent spirits to hunt them down.

599
00:46:57,400 --> 00:46:59,650
Do you happen to know or have heard

600
00:46:59,670 --> 00:47:01,720
any stories about sorcerers around here?

601
00:47:04,250 --> 00:47:05,190
Well...

602
00:47:06,390 --> 00:47:08,520
there are a few sorcerers

603
00:47:08,540 --> 00:47:11,400
who work for powerful people.

604
00:47:12,450 --> 00:47:13,510
Which means...

605
00:47:13,960 --> 00:47:15,450
those kids

606
00:47:16,090 --> 00:47:19,550
might have gotten involved
in something they shouldn't have.

607
00:47:23,710 --> 00:47:24,490
Well...

608
00:47:27,280 --> 00:47:28,280
Master,

609
00:47:28,490 --> 00:47:31,480
lives are on the line here.

610
00:47:32,750 --> 00:47:35,390
It's better to let us handle this.

611
00:47:38,330 --> 00:47:39,620
I've come this far.

612
00:47:41,460 --> 00:47:43,240
I have to save them no matter what.

613
00:47:58,490 --> 00:47:59,290
Jet,

614
00:47:59,850 --> 00:48:01,610
why did Kachen want to meet here?

615
00:48:04,130 --> 00:48:06,340
Surprise!

616
00:48:06,360 --> 00:48:08,910
[K-2101 Bangkok]

617
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:10,490
What?

618
00:48:10,640 --> 00:48:11,460
What?

619
00:48:11,950 --> 00:48:13,780
Paran bought this car for you to use

620
00:48:13,800 --> 00:48:15,160
whenever you're in Bangkok.

621
00:48:16,450 --> 00:48:18,130
- This is my car?
- Yeah.

622
00:48:18,150 --> 00:48:19,990
[K-2101 Bangkok]

623
00:48:25,060 --> 00:48:26,330
Is it really my car?

624
00:48:35,180 --> 00:48:36,760
Didn't he mention it to you?

625
00:48:42,760 --> 00:48:44,710
Congratulations, Khem.

626
00:48:47,020 --> 00:48:48,600
Want to take it for a maiden spin?

627
00:48:51,810 --> 00:48:53,010
I don't know how to drive.

628
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:55,590
Could you drive for me?

629
00:48:56,970 --> 00:48:57,770
Sure.

630
00:49:00,350 --> 00:49:01,720
Hey, Kachen.

631
00:49:02,190 --> 00:49:03,630
Are you going back to
Ubon Ratchathani soon?

632
00:49:03,910 --> 00:49:05,920
If you do, don't mention
anything to my mom yet.

633
00:49:11,900 --> 00:49:13,410
Alright, got it.

634
00:49:13,540 --> 00:49:15,070
I'll stay out of it for now.

635
00:49:16,220 --> 00:49:17,800
Should I even bother going back?

636
00:49:18,010 --> 00:49:19,690
Even if I do, no one's there.

637
00:49:21,020 --> 00:49:22,000
Honestly, though,

638
00:49:22,420 --> 00:49:24,710
I thought Paran was gonna turn down work

639
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:28,460
after the monk warned him
about the misfortune coming his way.

640
00:49:33,850 --> 00:49:36,080
The monk? You mean Monk Kasem?

641
00:49:46,480 --> 00:49:47,410
Kachen.

642
00:49:47,980 --> 00:49:48,860
Yes?

643
00:49:48,930 --> 00:49:50,340
What did he say?

644
00:49:58,250 --> 00:49:59,440
Ouch, take it easy.

645
00:50:03,910 --> 00:50:05,350
Thank you so much, Master.

646
00:50:07,240 --> 00:50:08,200
I'll take my leave now.

647
00:50:11,560 --> 00:50:13,440
- Hello? It's done.
- That auntie...

648
00:50:13,460 --> 00:50:14,870
Master is so handsome!

649
00:50:14,900 --> 00:50:17,420
The other guy didn't have
a clue about anything.

650
00:50:21,240 --> 00:50:23,310
Guess I can't go celebrate
with you anymore.

651
00:50:23,570 --> 00:50:26,110
I'll have to hit the town
and find someone

652
00:50:26,130 --> 00:50:28,490
to soothe this sore waist of mine.

653
00:50:30,730 --> 00:50:32,120
Don't get too wild.

654
00:50:32,960 --> 00:50:34,600
You're not that young anymore.

655
00:50:36,530 --> 00:50:39,560
You would do well
to heed his words, Kachen.

656
00:50:40,410 --> 00:50:42,590
Especially in the coming year.

657
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:46,670
I see the shadow of ill fortune
hanging over you.

658
00:50:47,670 --> 00:50:49,340
But not just you...

659
00:50:57,110 --> 00:50:59,040
The wedding day
is drawing near now, isn't it?

660
00:51:01,180 --> 00:51:02,200
Yes, Monk Kasem.

661
00:51:02,770 --> 00:51:05,290
If you complete your pilgrimage early,

662
00:51:05,980 --> 00:51:07,280
please honor us with your presence.

663
00:51:09,600 --> 00:51:11,950
I may not be able
to attend your wedding,

664
00:51:12,300 --> 00:51:13,460
but...

665
00:51:15,050 --> 00:51:17,470
I'd like to offer
my blessings in advance.

666
00:51:17,670 --> 00:51:19,910
May you and Khem

667
00:51:20,450 --> 00:51:22,940
love and cherish each other
for years to come.

668
00:51:24,820 --> 00:51:25,960
Also...

669
00:51:29,980 --> 00:51:32,220
take good care of yourself.

670
00:51:33,500 --> 00:51:35,550
Don't meddle in things

671
00:51:36,020 --> 00:51:38,340
that are not yours to deal with.

672
00:51:38,700 --> 00:51:40,450
This misfortune hanging over you

673
00:51:43,520 --> 00:51:45,430
is grave enough to cost you your life.

674
00:51:51,170 --> 00:51:53,420
He probably didn't want you to worry.

675
00:51:53,740 --> 00:51:54,920
I'm sorry

676
00:51:55,830 --> 00:51:57,340
that you had to find out from me.

677
00:52:11,320 --> 00:52:12,350
Hurry.

678
00:52:15,180 --> 00:52:16,120
Shit!

679
00:52:20,150 --> 00:52:21,150
What the hell is this?

680
00:52:30,930 --> 00:53:05,800
[Incanting]

681
00:53:05,830 --> 00:53:07,120
What should we do, Khem?

682
00:53:07,310 --> 00:53:08,910
We can still change our minds.

683
00:53:09,010 --> 00:53:10,460
Should we help Master instead?

684
00:53:10,590 --> 00:53:12,960
Yeah, I'll go with you anyway.

685
00:53:17,860 --> 00:53:19,350
There's nothing we can do to help.

686
00:53:19,490 --> 00:53:20,560
We should go to the set.

687
00:53:20,580 --> 00:53:22,570
They're waiting for our help, too.

688
00:53:22,720 --> 00:53:23,840
Are you really okay?

689
00:53:26,900 --> 00:53:27,640
Yeah.

690
00:53:28,850 --> 00:53:30,380
I trust Master.

691
00:53:38,890 --> 00:53:47,310
[Incanting]

692
00:54:19,480 --> 00:54:21,200
Please grant me the chance

693
00:54:22,460 --> 00:54:25,560
to return to my beloved.

694
00:55:25,940 --> 00:55:27,140
I've had this strange feeling

695
00:55:27,170 --> 00:55:29,190
ever since we got here.

696
00:55:30,610 --> 00:55:33,750
The life force is being concealed
by numerous spirits.

697
00:55:33,780 --> 00:55:34,900
Master...

698
00:55:35,640 --> 00:55:36,740
I feel like he's...

699
00:55:36,770 --> 00:55:37,590
Master!

700
00:55:39,060 --> 00:55:40,180
I promised you

701
00:55:40,700 --> 00:55:42,210
I'd make it back alive.

702
00:55:42,990 --> 00:55:44,980
May the merit you have earned

703
00:55:45,160 --> 00:55:47,530
guide you to a better realm,

704
00:55:47,710 --> 00:55:49,610
and may you leave this world
free of all worries.

705
00:55:52,270 --> 00:55:55,420
♪ We're soulmates, together we'll stay
(Together we'll stay) ♪

706
00:55:55,450 --> 00:55:58,640
♪ Right by each other's side till
our dying day (Till our dying day) ♪

707
00:55:58,670 --> 00:56:04,920
♪ Our love will never die
or wither away ♪

708
00:56:04,950 --> 00:56:08,240
♪ Life may not go our way,
(Go our way) ♪

709
00:56:08,270 --> 00:56:11,430
♪ And the world
can be cruel some days, ♪

710
00:56:11,460 --> 00:56:18,660
♪ But we'll hold each other
till the end of days ♪

711
00:56:19,040 --> 00:56:22,100
[The UNCUT version of Khemjira Forever]

712
00:56:22,130 --> 00:56:24,270
[is exclusively available
on iQIYI and iQ.com]

713
00:56:41,420 --> 00:56:50,030
♪ Till the end of days ♪
